          "text": "Lewy bodies",
          "is_correct": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "ANSWER: A Reduction of weight and blood flow are features of the normal aging brain. Additionally, there is widening of sulci and associated ventricular enlargement. Lewy bodies are inclusions found in neurons of individuals with Parkinson's disease, Parkinson-plus syndromes, and dementia with Lewy bodies.",
