      ],
      "explanation": "ANSWER: B Myelin is formed in the CNS by oligodendrocytes. Schwann cells form myelin in the peripheral nervous system (PNS). Microglia are derived from macrophages and act as scavengers that eliminate debris from neuronal injury and death. Astrocytes are cells that form the blood-brain barrier, remove certain neurotransmitters from the synaptic cleft, buffer extracellular potassium concentration, and serve a nutritive function.",
